		{"id":"enum-plan","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Plan|Enumeration Plan]]","x":-1500,"y":-300,"width":220,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-heading","type":"text","text":"## Enumeration","x":-1750,"y":-300,"width":180,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-nmap","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/nmap|Nmap]]","x":-1210,"y":-300,"width":180,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-ports","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Ports-Actions|Ports → Actions]]","x":-960,"y":-300,"width":140,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-smb","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/SMB enum|SMB Enumeration]]","x":-650,"y":-285,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"enum-web","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Web enum|Web Enumeration]]","x":-650,"y":-370,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"enum-snmp","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/snmp enum|SNMP Enumeration]]","x":-650,"y":-195,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"choose","type":"text","text":"## Identify OS and attack surface\n\nMap every port to a service, version, hostname, and next action.","x":-240,"y":-290,"width":480,"height":120,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# OSCP Standalone Box Methodology\n\n**Enumerate → foothold → stabilize/transfer → escalate → proof**\n\nRecord credentials, usernames, ports, failed attempts, and evidence as you work.","x":-560,"y":-720,"width":800,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"shell","type":"text","text":"[[Shell & upgrade/Intro|Shell and Upgrade]]","x":740,"y":-280,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-ad-note","type":"text","text":"[[ZeroLogon and noPac|ZeroLogon, noPac, and Certifried notes]]","x":800,"y":4420,"width":840,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-zerologon","type":"text","text":"## ZeroLogon — CVE-2020-1472\n\nUnpatched Netlogon secure channel weakness on a domain controller → domain compromise without credentials. Treat as high impact and verify patch state carefully.","x":800,"y":4610,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-nopac","type":"text","text":"## noPac — CVE-2021-42278 + CVE-2021-42287\n\nsAMAccountName spoofing chain → Domain Admin from a low-privileged domain user when prerequisites and missing patches align.","x":800,"y":4890,"width":840,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-certifried","type":"text","text":"## Certifried — CVE-2022-26923\n\nADCS plus machine-account identity spoofing → authenticate as a domain controller and escalate. Requires an applicable CA/template and account-control conditions.","x":800,"y":5160,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cve-local-check","type":"text","text":"## Prefer simpler paths first\n\nCheck sudo rights, SUID/capabilities, writable services/scripts, credentials, cron/systemd jobs, and exposed local services before choosing a risky kernel exploit.","x":-420,"y":5490,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cve-ad-links","type":"text","text":"## Detailed playbooks\n\n[[Active Directory/Attack-Phases/Phase-2-3/ZeroLogon — Unauthenticated Domain Admin (CVE-2020-1472)|ZeroLogon playbook]]\n\n[[Active Directory/Attack-Phases/Phase-2-3/noPac- SamAccountName Spoofing — Low-Priv User to DA (CVE-2021-42278 + CVE-2021-42287)|noPac playbook]]\n\n[[Active Directory/Attack-Phases/Phase-2-3/ADCS — Active Directory Certificate Services|ADCS playbook]]","x":800,"y":5440,"width":840,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-reference","type":"text","text":"[[CVEs|Open the complete CVE shortlist]]","x":-410,"y":5920,"width":820,"height":110,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-result","type":"text","text":"# Record the outcome\n\nDocument the detected version, supporting evidence, exploit source, modifications, command used, returned security context, and cleanup. If the match is uncertain, return to enumeration.","x":-500,"y":6140,"width":1000,"height":190,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cve-ad-head","type":"text","text":"# Active Directory CVEs\n\nConfirm the domain controller, patch state, authentication level, and ADCS availability before selecting a chain.","x":800,"y":4200,"width":840,"height":150,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-local-head","type":"text","text":"# Local root candidates\n\nConsider these after obtaining a shell and checking the installed package/kernel versions and exploit prerequisites.","x":-420,"y":4200,"width":840,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-local-userland","type":"text","text":"## Userland / setuid paths\n\n- **CVE-2021-3156 Baron Samedit** — sudo before 1.9.5p2 → local root\n- **CVE-2021-4034 PwnKit** — vulnerable pkexec/polkit → local root\n- **CVE-2023-4911 Looney Tunables** — vulnerable glibc `ld.so` on affected distributions → local root","x":-420,"y":4440,"width":840,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-local-kernel","type":"text","text":"## Kernel paths\n\n- **CVE-2022-0847 Dirty Pipe** — affected Linux kernels in the 5.8–5.16.11 range → local root\n- **CVE-2016-5195 Dirty COW** — affected older kernels → local root\n\nKernel exploits can destabilize a host; confirm the exact build and constraints first.","x":-420,"y":4820,"width":840,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-local-enum","type":"text","text":"## Evidence to collect\n\n`uname -a` · `/etc/os-release` · package versions · glibc version · architecture · mount options · available compiler/tooling","x":-420,"y":5220,"width":840,"height":170,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-win","type":"text","text":"## Windows network services\n\n- **MS17-010 EternalBlue** — Windows 7 / Server 2008 R2, SMBv1 → SYSTEM\n- **CVE-2019-0708 BlueKeep** — Windows 7 / Server 2008, RDP → RCE/SYSTEM\n- **CVE-2020-0796 SMBGhost** — SMBv3 compression, Windows 10 / Server 2019 → RCE/SYSTEM\n- **CVE-2021-1675 PrintNightmare** — Windows print spooler → SYSTEM/RCE","x":-1640,"y":4420,"width":840,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-web","type":"text","text":"## Web and application servers\n\n- **CVE-2021-41773** — Apache 2.4.49 path traversal → RCE\n- **CVE-2021-44228 Log4Shell** — Log4j 2.x → RCE\n- **CVE-2022-26134** — Confluence OGNL injection → RCE\n- **CVE-2021-22205** — GitLab ExifTool avatar upload → RCE","x":-1640,"y":4800,"width":840,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-enterprise","type":"text","text":"## Enterprise applications\n\n- **ProxyShell** — CVE-2021-34473 / 34523 / 31207, Exchange → RCE/SYSTEM\n- **ProxyLogon** — CVE-2021-26855, Exchange → pre-auth RCE\n- **CVE-2023-22515 / 22518** — Confluence access-control failure → admin creation / RCE\n- **CVE-2023-38408** — OpenSSH < 9.3p2 with forwarded ssh-agent → RCE","x":-1640,"y":5180,"width":840,"height":330,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-check","type":"text","text":"## Gate before execution\n\nExact build confirmed? Required service/feature enabled? Network path reachable? Exploit source reviewed? Crash or cleanup risk understood?","x":-1640,"y":5560,"width":840,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"reset","type":"text","text":"## If progress stalls\n\nReturn to enumeration. Recheck UDP, virtual hosts, authenticated features, files/metadata, credential reuse, local-only services, and exact versions. Avoid guessing exploits without evidence.","x":-450,"y":2940,"width":900,"height":170,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-head","type":"text","text":"# Remote exploitation\n\nUse only when enumeration proves the exposed product and vulnerable version or configuration.","x":-1640,"y":4200,"width":840,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-verify","type":"text","text":"## 3. Verify the candidate\n\nConfirm affected versions, prerequisites, authentication, exploit reliability, and required edits. Read the code before running it.","x":-10,"y":3560,"width":480,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-fingerprint","type":"text","text":"## 1. Fingerprint precisely\n\nRecord product, exact version/build, OS and architecture, exposed feature, and reachable port.","x":-1120,"y":3570,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-searchsploit","type":"text","text":"[[Searchsploit|2. Searchsploit commands]]\n\nSearch locally, open the source, then copy only the candidate you intend to inspect.","x":-570,"y":3570,"width":450,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-classify","type":"text","text":"## 4. Choose the matching path\n\nIs this remote code execution, local privilege escalation, or an Active Directory escalation?","x":580,"y":3575,"width":450,"height":150,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-intro","type":"text","text":"[[Definitions/Common CVEs & Exploits/Intro|Start here: CVE safety and selection]]","x":-1640,"y":3600,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-validate","type":"text","text":"## 5. Validate safely\n\nSet the exact target and callback values, prefer a non-destructive check, capture evidence, and stop if behavior differs from expectations.","x":1130,"y":3560,"width":500,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cve-title","type":"text","text":"# Common CVEs & Exploits\n\n**Fingerprint → match exact version → inspect exploit → validate safely → document result**\n\nUse this map only against systems you are authorized to test.","x":-390,"y":3240,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"pa-title","type":"text","text":"# Password attacks\n\n[[Definitions/Password attacks/Intro|Concepts and attack selection]]\n\nIdentify the credential material first, then choose the least noisy effective path.","x":2660,"y":470,"width":720,"height":170,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-start","type":"text","text":"## What do you have?\n\nA stolen hash, a live login service, or an opportunity to capture/relay NTLM authentication?","x":2660,"y":720,"width":720,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"pa-hash","type":"text","text":"# Hash obtained\n\nPreserve the original and identify its type before cracking.","x":2660,"y":970,"width":500,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-modes","type":"text","text":"[[Definitions/Password attacks/Hash Mode Reference|Hashcat Mode Reference]]\n\nNTLM `1000` · NetNTLMv2 `5600` · Kerberoast `13100` · AS-REP `18200` · SHA512crypt `1800`","x":2660,"y":1170,"width":500,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-crack","type":"text","text":"## Crack offline\n\n`hashcat -m <MODE> hashes.txt rockyou.txt`\n\nFast, silent, and no account lockouts. Add targeted rules only when evidence supports them.","x":2660,"y":1400,"width":500,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-result","type":"text","text":"# Credential or access obtained\n\nMap it to a user, host, service, and privilege level. Validate carefully, check permitted reuse, and preserve a clean evidence trail.","x":3040,"y":1720,"width":960,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"pa-live","type":"text","text":"# Live login service\n\nConfirm the protocol, username format, failure response, authorization, and lockout policy.","x":3240,"y":970,"width":500,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"pa-online","type":"text","text":"[[Definitions/Password attacks/Online Brute Force|Online Brute Force & Password Spraying]]\n\nOne user + wordlist → targeted brute force\nMany users + one password → controlled spray","x":3240,"y":1180,"width":500,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"pa-throttle","type":"text","text":"## Control authentication noise\n\nThrottle requests and stop on lockouts or unexpected impact. Prefer low-volume validation over indiscriminate guessing.","x":3240,"y":1420,"width":500,"height":150,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-ntlm","type":"text","text":"# NTLM authentication path\n\n[[Definitions/Password attacks/NTLM Capture & Relay|NTLM Capture & Relay]]","x":3820,"y":970,"width":540,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-capture","type":"text","text":"## Capture or crack\n\nRun Responder on the correct interface. Save the NetNTLM challenge-response and crack it offline with mode `5600`.","x":3820,"y":1170,"width":540,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-signing","type":"text","text":"## Check before relay\n\nGenerate a relay list. Relay only to hosts where SMB signing is not required. Captured NetNTLM is not an NTLM password hash.","x":3820,"y":1400,"width":540,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-reset","type":"text","text":"## If the path fails\n\nRecheck hash type and formatting, usernames/domains, service responses, lockout policy, SMB signing, and whether captured material is crackable or relayable.","x":3040,"y":1990,"width":960,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ft-title","type":"text","text":"# File Transfer\n\nChoose the direction of transfer, then open the corresponding note.","x":3390,"y":2860,"width":520,"height":140,"color":"3"},
